{
  "dom_id": "step-q68952",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "${2}^{3}\\cdot {(3\\cdot 2)}^{4}=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the second factor using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n{2}^{3}\\cdot {(3\\cdot 2)}^{4}={2}^{3}\\cdot {3}^{4}\\cdot {2}^{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the product rule for exponents, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{3}\\cdot {3}^{4}\\cdot {2}^{4} & ={2}^{3}\\cdot {2}^{4}\\cdot {3}^{4} \\\\  & ={2}^{3+4}\\cdot {3}^{4} \\\\  & ={2}^{7}\\cdot {3}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
